[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    - Since \( 8 \equiv 2 \pmod{6} \):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      2x \equiv 53 \pmod{6}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      53 \div 6 = 8 \text{ with a remainder of } 5 \Rightarrow 53 \equiv 5 \pmod{6}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      So,
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      2x \equiv 5 \pmod{6}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    - Multiply both sides by the modular inverse of 2 modulo 6, which is not defined since 2 and 6 are not coprime. Instead, test values of \( x \) starting from 26 upwards:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    
