[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 2. **After finding the additional 53 coins, the total number of coins becomes \( 7n + 53 \).**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 3. **You want to redistribute these coins into all eight bags such that each bag has the same number of coins. So, \( 7n + 53 \) should be divisible by 8. Mathematically, this means:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    7n + 53 \equiv 0 \pmod{8}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    Simplifying the equation:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    7n \equiv -53 \pmod{8}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    Since \(-53 \mod 8\) is equivalent to:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    -53 \mod 8 = -53 + 8 \times 7 = -53 + 56 = 3
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    Therefore:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    7n \equiv 3 \pmod{8}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 4. **To solve for \( n \), find the multiplicative inverse of 7 modulo 8. Since \( 7 \equiv -1 \pmod{8} \), the inverse of 7 modulo 8 is also -1, which is equivalent to 7 modulo 8. Therefore:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    n \equiv 3 \times 7 \pmod{8}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    \[
