[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      k = 1: \quad n = 8(1) + 7 = 15
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      k = 2: \quad n = 8(2) + 7 = 23
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      \vdots
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    We need the smallest \( n > 200 \):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    n = 8k + 7 > 200 \implies 8k > 193 \implies k > \frac{193}{8} = 24.125 \implies k \geq 25
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    So, the smallest integer \( k \) is 25:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    n = 8(25) + 7 = 200 + 7 = 207
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 8. **Calculate the Total Number of Coins Initially**:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    7n + 53 = 7(207) + 53 = 1449 + 53 = 1502
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 9. **Verify the Solution**:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    - Distribute \( 1502 \) coins into 8 bags:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      m = \frac{1502}{8} = 187.75 \quad \text{(Not an integer)}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    We find the correct smallest \( n \):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    \text{Use } k=3: n = 8(3) + 7 = 29
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    \[
