[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    - **Total number of ways to choose any 5 members out of 14**:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      \binom{14}{5}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    - **Subcases**:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      We consider two scenarios:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      a. **Subcommittee consists only of Republicans**:  
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m         \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m         \binom{8}{5} \text{ (choosing 5 Republicans out of 8)}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m         \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      b. **Subcommittee consists only of Democrats**:  
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m         \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m         \binom{6}{5} \text{ (choosing 5 Democrats out of 6)}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m         \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      However, we must subtract these two scenarios from the total possible combinations to find the favorable ones.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      The number of ways to choose a subcommittee with no Democrats:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      \binom{8}{5} = \frac{8!}{5!(8-5)!} = \frac{8 \times 7 \times 6 \times 5 \times 4}{5 \times 4 \times 3 \times 2 \times 1} = 56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      The number of ways to choose a subcommittee with no Republicans:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      \binom{6}{5} = \frac{6!}{5!(6-5)!} = \frac{6}{1} = 6
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      Using the principle of inclusion-exclusion, the number of favorable combinations (i.e., at least one member from each party) is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      \binom{14}{5} - \binom{8}{5} - \binom{6}{5} = \binom{14}{5} - \binom{8}{5} - \binom{6}{5}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 5. **Calculate Each Component**:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    - \( \binom{14}{5} \):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      \binom{14}{5} = \frac{14!}{5!(14-5)!} = \frac{14 \times 13 \times 12 \times 11 \times 10}{5 \times 4 \times 3 \times 2 \times 1} = 2002
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    - Therefore:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      \binom{14}{5} - \binom{8}{5} - \binom{6}{5} = 2002 - 56 - 6 = 1940
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m      
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m So, the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members with at least one member from each party is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m \boxed{1940}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m \]
