[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 4. **Total Number of Ways to Choose 5 Members from 14 Members**:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    This can be calculated using combinations:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    \binom{14}{5} = \frac{14!}{5!(14-5)!} = \frac{14 \times 13 \times 12 \times 11 \times 10}{5 \times 4 \times 3 \times 2 \times 1} = 2002
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 5. **Count the Number of Subcommittees with Only Republicans**:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    If the subcommittee consists of only Republicans, we choose 5 out of 8 Republicans:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    \binom{8}{5} = \frac{8!}{5!(8-5)!} = \frac{8 \times 7 \times 6 \times 5 \times 4}{5 \times 4 \times 3 \times 2 \times 1} = 56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 6. **Count the Number of Subcommittees with Only Democrats**:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    Similarly, if the subcommittee consists of only Democrats, we choose 5 out of 6 Democrats:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    \binom{6}{5} = \frac{6!}{5!(6-5)!} = \frac{6 \times 5!}{5! \times 1} = 6
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 7. **Subtract the Invalid Combinations**:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    The number of subcommittees that do not meet the condition (either entirely Republicans or entirely Democrats) is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    \text{Number of invalid subcommittees} = \binom{8}{5} + \binom{6}{5} = 56 + 6 = 62
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 8. **Calculate the Number of Valid Subcommittees**:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    To get the number of subcommittees with at least one member from each party, we subtract the invalid cases from the total number of possible subcommittees:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    \text{Number of valid subcommittees} = \binom{14}{5} - (\binom{8}{5} + \binom{6}{5})
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    Substituting the values:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    \text{Number of valid subcommittees} = 2002 - 62 = 1940
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m ### Conclusion:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m Thus, the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members with at least one member from each party is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m \boxed{1940}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m \]
