[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 2. **Use the Complement Principle**:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    Instead of directly calculating the number of ways to form a subcommittee with at least one member from each party, it's easier to use the complement principle:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    - Calculate the total number of ways to choose any subcommittee of 5 members without any restrictions.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    - Subtract the number of all-republican or all-democratic subcommittees from this total.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 3. **Calculate the Total Number of Ways to Choose Any 5 Members**:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    The total number of ways to choose 5 members out of 14 (8 Republicans + 6 Democrats) is given by the combination formula:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    \[
