[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m A Senate committee has 8 Republicans and 6 Democrats.  In how many ways can we form a subcommittee of 5 members that has at least one member from each party?
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{}.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m assistant
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m output:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m To determine the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members that includes at least one member from each party (Republicans and Democrats), we can use the principle of complementary counting.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m Here’s how we’ll solve the problem step-by-step:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m ### Given:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m - Number of Republicans = 8
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m - Number of Democrats = 6
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m - Subcommittee size = 5
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m ### Total number of ways to choose any 5 members from the committee without any restrictions:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m We can choose any 5 members from the 14 (8 Republicans + 6 Democrats). This is a combination problem:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m \text{Total number of ways} = \binom{14}{5}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m Calculating this:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m \binom{14}{5} = \frac{14!}{5!(14-5)!} = \frac{14!}{5! \cdot 9!} = 2002
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m ### Case 1: All members are from Republicans
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m To form a subcommittee consisting only of Republicans, we choose all 5 members from the 8 Republicans:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m \text{Number of ways} = \binom{8}{5}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m \binom{8}{5} = \frac{8!}{5!(8-5)!} = \frac{8!}{5! \cdot 3!} = 56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m ### Case 2: All members are from Democrats
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m Similarly, to form a subcommittee consisting only of Democrats, we choose all 5 members from the 6 Democrats:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m \text{Number of ways} = \binom{6}{5}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m \binom{6}{5} = \frac{6!}{5!(6-5)!} = \frac{6!}{5! \cdot 1!} = 6
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m ### Applying the complementary counting principle:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m To find the number of valid subcommittees that include members from both parties (i.e., at least one Republican and one Democrat), we subtract the invalid cases (all Republicans or all Democrats) from the total possible combinations.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m So, we calculate:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m \text{Number of valid subcommittees} = \binom{14}{5} - \left( \binom{8}{5} + \binom{6}{5} \right)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m = 2002 - (56 + 6)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m = 2002 - 62
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m = 1940
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m Thus, the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members that includes at least one member from each party is \(\boxed{1940}\).
