[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m To find the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members from a Senate committee consisting of 8 Republicans and 6 Democrats, such that the subcommittee has at least one member from each party, we can follow these steps:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m ### **Given:**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m - Number of Republicans (R) = 8
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m - Number of Democrats (D) = 6
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m - Size of the subcommittee (n) = 5
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m ### **Objective:**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m We want to form a subcommittee with at least one Republican and at least one Democrat. This means we cannot form a subcommittee consisting entirely of Republicans or entirely of Democrats.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m ### **Approach:**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m To solve this problem, we can use the **inclusion-exclusion principle**:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 1. **Total number of ways to choose any 5 members from the committee without any restrictions.**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m \text{Total ways} = \binom{14}{5} = \frac{14!}{5!(14-5)!} = \frac{14 \times 13 \times 12 \times 11 \times 10}{5 \times 4 \times 3 \times 2 \times 1} = 2002
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 2. **Subtract the number of all-Republican and all-Democrat subcommittees:**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m - Number of ways to choose a subcommittee of 5 Republicans:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m \binom{8}{5} = \frac{8!}{5!(8-5)!} = \frac{8 \times 7 \times 6}{3 \times 2 \times 1} = 56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m   
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m - Number of ways to choose a subcommittee of 5 Democrats:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m \binom{6}{5} = \frac{6!}{5!(6-5)!} = 6
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 3. **Apply the inclusion-exclusion principle:**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m To get the number of valid subcommittees with at least one Republican and one Democrat:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m \text{Number of valid subcommittees} = \text{Total ways} - \text{All Republicans} - \text{All Democrats}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m = \binom{14}{5} - \binom{8}{5} - \binom{6}{5}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m = 2002 - 56 - 6
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m = 2002 - 62
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m = 1940
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m \]
