[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 1. **Total Members**:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    - Republicans: 8
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    - Democrats: 6
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    - Total members: 8 + 6 = 14
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 2. **Total Ways to Choose 5 Members**:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    - The total number of ways to choose 5 members out of 14 without any restrictions is given by the combination formula:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    \binom{14}{5} = \frac{14!}{5!(14-5)!} = \frac{14 \times 13 \times 12 \times 11 \times 10}{5 \times 4 \times 3 \times 2 \times 1} = 2002
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m 3. **Using Complementary Counting**:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=88790)[0m    Instead of directly counting the number of valid subcommittees with at least one Republican and one Democrat, it's easier to subtract the invalid cases (i.e., all members are Republicans or all are Democrats).
